From e0455344828a71364a9aa1d310ead4cb9b453b1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Kanis <lars@greiz-reinsdorf.de>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:59:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: Allow YJIT on MINGW toolset

YJIT on Windows was introduced in https://github.com/ruby/ruby/pull/19114
for MSVC on x86_64 only. But is works with a few adjustments on MINGW as well.

Currently the libruby dll exports leaks symbols from rust on x64, so that the leak
check is bypassed for now.

I divided the SEH unwind tests into C++ standard based and MSVC custom syntax
extension.
